  "Source": "E. R. Brennan, \"Multi-Layer All-Dielectric Reflection Filters,\" M.S. thesis (Physics), Polytechnic Institute of Brooklyn (1963), thesis adviser A. Zajac. No doi. - Sec. II.A, pp. 2 and 4",
  "Notes": "Step 2: quarter-wave ZnS then quarter-wave MgF2 on the ruby face (destructive interference step of the build-up)\nSpecification: Intermediate step of the build-up; reflectance at 694.3 nm.\nReported: Reflectance is reduced to 6.2 % at 694.3 nm, normal incidence (pp. 2-4).\nNotes: Ruby (assumed n = 1.76) is the incident medium and air the exit medium; layer 1 (ZnS) is on the ruby face, MgF2 faces air. An admittance check with n0 = 1.76 gives 6.2 %, matching.\nLayers from Sec. II.A, pp. 2 and 4; layer 1 faces the incident medium.\nChecked with ThinFilmDesigner (2026-10-21), agrees with the paper: ours R 6.18 % at 694.3 nm; paper R 6.2 % (pp. 2-4).",
